# Provenance guard — defect-isola-runtime-live-local-commit-tracks-secret-backup-files-2026-08-06.
# Operational snapshots written beside live source on the deployment host were
# committed to a local-only branch; two carried real credentials. These patterns
# are deliberately narrow: each requires a backup marker in the filename, so no
# legitimate source, migration, fixture or configuration file is hidden.
/.env.pre-*
/docker-compose.yml.pre-*
backend/**/*.bak-*
backend/**/*.pre-*-bak
docker-compose.override.yml.*-backup

# Scoped-reset operational database dumps (pg_dump output written beside live
# source on the deployment host by the 2026-07-25 scoped-reset runbook). These
# are secret-bearing by default -- they carry real tenant rows -- and must never
# be committed. Scoped to the rooted `backups/scoped-reset-*` prefix rather than
# a bare `*.dump`/`*.sql` glob so that migrations, fixtures and any legitimate
# SQL elsewhere in the tree stay visible to git.
/backups/scoped-reset-*/

# CC-created safety snapshots from rotation/migration work (per workspace-backup runbook)
*.bak
.bak-archive-*/
